# Dockerfile does `COPY backend/ .`, so without this, a local `docker build` bakes
# backend/.env (TICKETMASTER_API_KEY and, after issue #118, a real SENTRY_DSN) plus
# a macOS-built virtualenv into the image. Production is unaffected — Railway
# builds from GitHub, where .env is gitignored — but this matters for local
# rebuilds and the two-deletion opt-out verification (see backend/README.md).
**/.env
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
